  "answer_text": "In *The Vampire Diaries*, Elena's transformation into a vampire happens across two episodes:\n\n**Season 3, Episode 22 \u2013 \"The Departed\"**\nElena Gilbert begins her transition into a vampire during the Season 3 finale, **\"The Departed\"** (Episode 22), after drowning in a car accident while having vampire blood in her system. Rebekah deliberately causes the car to crash off Wickery Bridge. Stefan arrives in time, but Elena urges him to save Matt first \u2014 and by the time Stefan pulls Elena out of the water, she has already breathed her last.\n\nUnbeknownst to everyone, Elena had vampire blood in her system, as Dr. Meredith Fell had injected it into her to save her from fatal injuries inflicted by Klaus.\n\n**Season 4, Episode 1 \u2013 \"Growing Pains\"**\nHer full transformation occurs in Season 4, Episode 1 (\"Growing Pains\"), where she wakes up in transition and must make the difficult decision to complete the process by drinking human blood.\n\nNotably, she became a vampire despite never wanting to be one. She remained a vampire for all of Seasons 4, 5, and 6, only being cured back into a human at the end of Season 6.",
